.TH ONEKO 6
.SH NAME oneko
oneko displays a cat that wanders around the desktop on its own.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oneko
[\fB--help\fP] [\fB--monitor\fP \fIn\fP] [\fB--time\fP \fIn\fP]
[\fB--speed\fP \fIn\fP] [\fB--min-wait\fP \fIn\fP]
[\fB--max-wait\fP \fIn\fP] [\fB--bed\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I oneko
creates a small desktop pet. The cat alternates between waiting, wandering,
sleeping, and occasional zoomies. It does not follow the mouse cursor.
.SS Options
.TP
.B --help
Prints help message on usage.
.TP
.B --bed
Shows a draggable bed that the cat may occasionally visit.
.TP
.BI --monitor " number"
Restricts the cat and bed to the specified XRandR monitor.
.TP
.BI --time " microseconds"
Sets the animation interval. The default is 125000 microseconds.
.TP
.BI --speed " pixels"
Sets the maximum distance moved in one animation tick. The default is 13.
.TP
.BI --min-wait " seconds"
Sets the minimum idle time between walks.
.TP
.BI --max-wait " seconds"
Sets the maximum idle time between walks.
.TP
.B --noshape
Don't use SHAPE extension.
.TP
.BI --fg " color"
Foreground color.
.TP
.BI --bg " color"
Background color.
.SS Resources
Application name is "neko" and class name is "Oneko".
.TP
.B time
Sets interval timer in micro-second.
.TP
.B speed
Sets distance to jump in pixel.
.B noshape
Set ``True'' if you don't want to use SHAPE extension.
.TP
.B foreground
Foreground color.
.TP
.B background
Background color.
.SH Notes
While this program uses XGetDefault, be sure to use "neko.resouce" form.
option is enabled by default.
